.TH SHAREDROP 1 "November 2026" "ShareDrop 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sharedrop \- peer-to-peer streaming file, folder, and clipboard beam utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sharedrop
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sharedrop
is a zero-configuration, cross-platform command-line file transfer tool engineered for direct peer-to-peer streaming over WebRTC DataChannels (RFC 8831) with automatic dual-transport WebSocket relay fallback.
.PP
Peers sharing the same local area network (LAN) discover each other automatically through ephemeral signaling. Across distinct networks, carrier CGNATs, or firewalls, peers establish direct encrypted communication using 6-digit cryptographic pairing codes or 5-character public rooms.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send \fIPATH\fR | \fITEXT\fR
Stream a file, recursive directory tree, or text string to a target peer, room, or generate an ephemeral cloud drop.
.TP
.B receive \fICODE\fR | \fIURL\fR
Download and verify a file drop using a 6-character drop identifier or direct download URL.
.TP
.B status
Query server health, latency, active peers, and public telemetry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server " \fIURL\fR"
Target signaling server URL. Defaults to \fBhttps://sharedrop.sarthakml.in\fR or the value of \fBSHAREDROP_SERVER\fR.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-room " \fICODE\fR"
Join or target an ad-hoc 5-character public room (e.g. \fBK7M9P\fR).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " \fINAME\fR"
Custom peer display identifier for the transfer session.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " \fIDIR\fR"
Destination output directory for incoming downloads. Defaults to the current working directory.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ephemeral
Force an ephemeral HTTP fallback drop with a 15-minute Time-To-Live (TTL).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON output for automated scripting and CI/CD pipelines.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command synopsis and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output version information and exit.
.SH PROTOCOL & STREAMING
Transfers utilize a memory-bounded streaming pipeline:
.IP \(bu 2
Payloads are sliced into fixed \fB65,536-byte (64 KB)\fR frames.
.IP \(bu 2
Backpressure flow control enforces a high watermark of 2 MB and resumes transmission when \fBbufferedAmountLowThreshold\fR drops to \fB512 KB\fR, preventing kernel socket buffer bloat and client heap exhaustion.
.IP \(bu 2
Direct P2P connections enforce Datagram Transport Layer Security (\fBDTLS 1.2/1.3\fR) with \fBAES-GCM (256-bit)\fR payload encryption.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Upload a tarball to an ephemeral drop and render an ASCII QR code:
.RS
.nf
$ sharedrop send ./release-v1.0.tar.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Beam a file to a specific public room:
.RS
.nf
$ sharedrop send ./document.pdf --room TEAM1 --name "Sarthak-Terminal"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Download a file drop by code into a downloads directory:
.RS
.nf
$ sharedrop receive 7HJNYW -o ~/Downloads
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query production server telemetry:
.RS
.nf
$ sharedrop status --server https://sharedrop.sarthakml.in
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHAREDROP_SERVER
Default signaling server endpoint if not specified via \fB--server\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error (network failure, timeout, invalid code, or unhandled rejection).
